# Cloudflare Pages headers — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/

# Security headers on every response
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Revalidate HTML so a new deploy shows immediately (no stale edge copy)
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# ── CSS and JS: DECLARED, not inherited ─────────────────────────────────────
# 🔴 2026-08-04. These two classes had no rule here at all, which meant nothing
# in this repository chose a policy for them — the platform did.
#
# The trigger was the sibling property. `nikatru.com`'s zone had Browser Cache
# TTL 14400, and Cloudflare edge-caches .css and .js by extension, so anything
# of those types was stamped `max-age=14400` whatever the origin declared —
# which on subly.nikatru.com gave /flutter_bootstrap.js a four-hour browser
# cache against a declared `max-age=0`, hiding returning visitors from the
# force-update kill switch. That zone is now on "Respect Existing Headers".
#
# ⚠️ THIS IS A DIFFERENT ZONE and its dashboard is not readable from this
# repository, so nothing here claims to know its Browser Cache TTL setting.
# What was MEASURED, 2026-08-04, is the behaviour: `/icon-32.png` and
# `/rajasekar-v4.webp` both came back `cf-cache-status: HIT` carrying the
# `max-age=31536000, immutable` THIS FILE declares. An edge-cached response
# returning the origin's own value is a zone that is not overriding it. That is
# evidence, not a setting — the setting is only visible in the dashboard.
#
# Also measured here: this site serves NO external CSS or JS today (every page
# styles itself in an inline <style> block), and a path with no rule in this
# file gets the Pages default, which came back as
# `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` on sitemap.xml and llms.txt.
#
# So the two rules below change nothing that is served today. THAT IS THE
# POINT: a policy file has to declare the class BEFORE the first file of that
# class exists, or the first stylesheet ships on whatever the platform or the
# zone happens to be defaulting to that week.
#
# WHY REVALIDATE AND NOT `immutable`. The CSS these sites will serve once they
# migrate onto sites/_shared is `tokens.css` and `base.css` — STABLE names with
# CHANGING content. `tokens.css` is GENERATED by Style Dictionary out of
# packages/tokens (it changed today) and `base.css` is hand-edited; neither
# name moves when its bytes do. `immutable` on a stable name means a CSS fix
# never reaches anyone who has already visited — for a year, and without even a
# revalidation on an explicit reload.
#
# Declared at ANY DEPTH (`/*.css`, not `/assets/*.css`) on purpose: the gap
# being closed is a file arriving somewhere nobody wrote a rule for.
/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Long-cache immutable static assets — but ONLY names that carry a version.
# `rajasekar-v4.jpg` / `rajasekar-v4.webp` carry theirs IN THE NAME, which is
# what makes `immutable` correct for them: a new cut gets a new name, so no
# cached copy can ever be the wrong one.
#
# 🔴 FIXED 2026-08-21 — `/*.png` NO LONGER SAYS `immutable`. This root ships SIX
# .png files and NOT ONE of them carries a version token: `icon-16.png`,
# `icon-32.png`, `icon-192.png`, `icon-512.png`, `apple-touch-icon.png` and
# `og-image.png` (the whole .png inventory under sites/rajasekarselvam/,
# counted this run). They are STABLE names with CHANGING content, and
# `immutable` on a stable name does not merely extend freshness — it suppresses
# revalidation, so replaced bytes do not reach a returning visitor even on an
# explicit reload.
#
# ── LIVE, NOT LATENT: THIS HAS ALREADY FIRED ONCE ON THIS ROOT ──────────────
# The text below this rule used to end "left as-is DELIBERATELY", which invites
# the reading that nothing had happened yet. MEASURED 2026-08-21: commit
# a0e0f54, dated 2026-07-23, `feat(brand): refresh inline SVG favicons + nav
# logos, refresh RS icons`, replaced the BYTES of five of those six under the
# SAME filenames — apple-touch-icon.png 11128 -> 17631, icon-16.png 626 -> 699,
# icon-32.png 1423 -> 1627, icon-192.png 11868 -> 19596, icon-512.png
# 32233 -> 89028. Not one name moved. (og-image.png is the sixth and was not in
# that commit; it is unchanged since the migration commit a77cbe8.) So the
# re-cut this rule was deferring HAD ALREADY SHIPPED a month earlier, straight
# into a year-long immutable declaration.
#
# And the declaration is what this edge serves: the .css/.js note above records
# `/icon-32.png` coming back `cf-cache-status: HIT` carrying
# `max-age=31536000, immutable` on 2026-08-04 — twelve days AFTER that re-cut.
# ⚠️ That note is a DATED RECORD and is left unedited: its `/icon-32.png` half
# describes what this file declared UNTIL today, not what it declares below.
# Its `/rajasekar-v4.webp` half is unaffected — .webp still says `immutable`.
#
# ── THE REASONING THAT WAS WRONG, kept rather than deleted ──────────────────
# "Left as-is DELIBERATELY — they are the page's heaviest bytes and re-cutting
# them is the owner's call." Re-cutting the ARTWORK is the owner's call; that
# half was true and is untouched here. But re-cutting was never what this gap
# needed. Two different acts sat under one owner-gate, and the cheap one
# inherited the expensive one's veto. A Cache-Control value changes not one
# pixel and not one filename, so there is no brand question in it to defer.
# sites/nikatru/_headers decoupled exactly these two on 2026-08-21; this is the
# same decoupling, on the root that still had them joined.
#
# 🔴 NO RENAME IS PROPOSED HERE, and NOT because one is blocked. The frozen
# legal snapshots that killed the nikatru rename have no counterpart on this
# root — measured 2026-08-21: sites/rajasekarselvam/ has no legal/ tree at all,
# and the six names are referenced from three non-`_headers` files
# (index.html, 404.html, site.webmanifest). The rename is simply not NEEDED:
# the header fixes the same defect at a strictly lower cost, and for
# og-image.png a rename carries a real one — social platforms cache the card
# they scraped from the OLD URL and every link already shared points at it.
#
# ⚠️ WHAT THIS DOES NOT CATCH, so it is not read as a full repair:
#   · A browser that ALREADY took one of these icons under the immutable header
#     keeps it until its own year runs out — into 2027 for a visit made before
#     this deploy. Cache-Control governs responses served from now on; nothing
#     but a new URL reaches a client that is already frozen, and that client is
#     exactly the one the 2026-07-23 re-cut never reached. This closes the hole
#     ahead; it un-freezes nobody behind.
#   · It is a DECLARATION. What this zone's edge returns is not readable from
#     this repository — see the ⚠️ over the .css/.js rules. A zone Cache Rule
#     could still override it and nothing here would report that.
#   · /*.jpg, /*.webp and /*.svg are UNTOUCHED and keep `immutable`. jpg and
#     webp are rajasekar-v4's, whose name carries its version; no .svg is served
#     here today. If a STABLE-named .jpg/.webp/.svg ever lands on this root the
#     same argument applies to it unchanged, and assert-web-cache-policy.mjs
#     names such a file on every run rather than failing the build.
#
# THE COST, weighed rather than discovered later: a returning visitor now spends
# ONE conditional request per icon instead of zero, and the bytes still come
# from the local cache on the 304. That is the identical bargain /*.css and
# /*.js take above.
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/site.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
